    "result_text": "Done. All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` endpoint now rejects a create whose lower-cased email already belongs to another owner, responding **409**. I followed the existing telephone-uniqueness pattern:\n\n1. **`CheckOwnerEmailUnique.java`** \u2014 new pipeline step. Email is optional, so a blank/absent value skips the check. Otherwise it compares the request's email (already lower-cased by the preceding `NormalizeOwnerEmail` step) against every existing owner's email normalized the same way (`OwnerEmail.normalize`), throwing `DuplicateEmailException` on a match.\n\n2. **`DuplicateEmailException.java`** \u2014 checked exception so it routes to an escalation handler.\n\n3. **`DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with a `ProblemDetail` body, mirroring `DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler`.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** `...owner.DuplicateEmailException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to the handler.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted `checkEmailUnique` into the pipeline, after the telephone check (so email is already normalized) and before the household check, matching the existing ordering convention.\n\nThe new `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test passes, and the full suite is green.",
