        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the established conventions of this pipeline and mirrors the existing telephone-uniqueness feature almost exactly:\n\n- **Logic in the right unit.** `CheckOwnerEmailUnique` is a single-responsibility guard step, parallel to the sibling `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique`, and is wired as its own step in `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 correctly placed after `normalizeEmail` (so it compares the normalized form) and before `checkHousehold`/`build`, matching the AGENTS.md guidance to reject before constructing the entity.\n- **No duplication.** Email semantics (`isPresent`, `normalize`) are reused from the existing `OwnerEmail` single-source-of-truth helper rather than reinvented inline, and the handler reuses the shared `ProblemDetails.build`. The optional-email guard (`isPresent`) is the right difference from the telephone check, since email is optional while telephone is required.\n- **Nothing is becoming a catch-all.** A dedicated checked `DuplicateEmailException` + its own escalation YAML + a dedicated `DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler` follow the one-exception-one-handler pattern used by `DuplicateTelephoneException`/`DuplicateHouseholdException`, rather than overloading an existing exception or handler.\n- **Idiomatic and additive.** Naming (`Check<E>\u2026`, `Duplicate\u2026Exception`, `\u2026ExceptionHandler`), the `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` + `OwnerRepository` signature, the checked exception for escalation routing, and the YAML layout all match surrounding files. Javadoc documents ordering and rationale consistent with the neighbors.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this entirely natural \u2014 it reads as the obvious counterpart to the telephone check already present."
